# {{SLUG}} agents

Config-only agent directories: each `agents/<id>/` holds a `manifest.json`, a
`site.yaml` validated against the reusable-agents schemas, an `AGENT.md`, and
3 to 7 goals bound to `RunResult.metrics`. The engines (price refresh, catalog
discovery, shelf audit, spec extraction, pick building, recall gate, goals
tracker, ...) live in reusable-agents; nothing here forks one.

- Create an agent with reusable-agents `install/create-agent.sh <id>
  {{SITE_DIR}}/agents ...` (see the reusable-agents CLAUDE.md, "Creating a new
  agent"). Ship every manifest with `"enabled": false` and no `cron_expr`
  until the operator approves it going live.
- `register-with-framework.sh` registers every directory here that has a
  manifest; run it only on the operator's go-ahead. The scaffold registers
  nothing.
- `implementer-scope.yaml` is the implementer block every per-site
  `site.yaml` that dispatches to the implementer must carry, and reusable-agents
  `examples/sites/{{SLUG}}.yaml` too (copy it in whole): it keeps `vendor/**`,
  `site.json`, `{{POLICY_FILE}}`, `deploy.env` and the gate policy
  (`tests/ui/gate.config.ts`) out of every dispatch kind, and the page
  manifest out of deploy repairs, but only where it is applied: on the
  implementer's framework-chain path and by the deployer to its repairs. The
  implementer's default claude path commits without any scope check
  (reusable-agents `agents/implementer/README.md`, "Path scope"), so there
  those files and the gate wiring are protected only by instructions. The
  deploy gate's kit checks (`tests/run-local-suite.sh`: the manifest, then the
  kit release in reusable-agents) catch an edited `vendor/affiliate-kit` only
  while the shim itself is untouched and the claimed kit version is committed
  in reusable-agents; nothing in this repository catches an edited
  `site.json`, policy, gate policy or `deploy.env`.
- `deploy.env` and `vendor/affiliate-kit/deploy` are read from the **live
  checkout**, committed or not: the deployer gates and builds a clean checkout
  of the commit, but runs the push, deploy and rollback stages
  (`vendor/affiliate-kit/deploy/<cloud>/deploy.sh --env deploy.env`) in this
  repository's working tree. `deploy.env` sets `MIGRATE_COMMAND` (run with the
  owner's DSN), the container env, the replica counts and `SMOKE_PATHS`, so an
  uncommitted edit there ships with a release whose diff looks clean.
- **Prerequisite: keep this site's implementer dispatches disabled.** Register
  or enable no agent whose recommendations dispatch to the implementer for
  this site (the SEO opportunity agent, article proposals, head-to-heads,
  catalog audits) until either
  - the implementer's claude path applies this scope to its own sessions,
    reverting or refusing an excluded path in the working tree as well as in
    the commit (an edit left uncommitted still reaches the deploy stages), or
  - the reusable-agents deployer refuses a release whose diff since the last
    green deploy touches an excluded path, and also refuses while the live
    checkout's `deploy.env` or `vendor/affiliate-kit` differs from the commit
    it ships (or runs the push, deploy and rollback stages from its clean
    checkout)

  (reusable-agents `kits/affiliate-site/CHANGELOG.md`, "Known issues").
